    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["REG2", "FCC1", "NAVC1"],
      "pins": ["REG2.1", "FCC1.11", "FCC1.27", "FCC1.50", "FCC1.75", "FCC1.100", "NAVC1.19", "NAVC1.32", "NAVC1.48", "NAVC1.64"],
      "nets": ["+3.3V", "+3V3", "unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)", "unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad27)", "unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad50)", "unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad75)", "unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad100)", "unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)", "unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad32)", "unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad48)", "unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad64)"],
      "observed": "REG2.1 drives +3.3V, while +3V3 is a separate net; none of the FCC1 or NAVC1 VDD pins is connected to either rail. NAVC1.VBAT is on +3V3, but that is not the MCU's main supply.",
      "expected": "The regulated 3.3 V rail should supply the VDD pins of both MCUs, as specified. Their VDD pins should not be left unconnected.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"+3.3V\") ... (node (ref \"REG2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"OUT\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)\") (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"11\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)\") (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"19\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3.3V feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MCUs lack main power through their VDD pins, so the flight-control and navigation computers cannot operate as intended. The separately named 3.3 V rails also leave the regulated output disconnected from the +3V3 domain.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["FCC1", "UART3_FCC1"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.48", "FCC1.73", "UART3_FCC1.3", "UART3_FCC1.4"],
      "nets": ["UART3_TX_FCC", "UART3_RX_FCC"],
      "observed": "The net named UART3_TX_FCC connects FCC1 pin 48 (VCAP) to UART3_FCC1 pin 3; UART3_RX_FCC connects FCC1 pin 73 (VCAP) to UART3_FCC1 pin 4.",
      "expected": "UART connector signals should connect to UART-capable GPIO pins. MCU VCAP pins should be used for their required regulator decoupling, not routed as UART signals.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"UART3_RX_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"73\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")) ... (node (ref \"UART3_FCC1\") (pin \"4\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"UART3_TX_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")) ... (node (ref \"UART3_FCC1\") (pin \"3\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The UART3 connector is driven from the MCU's VCAP nodes rather than UART signals, preventing UART3 communication and potentially disrupting the MCU's internal regulator.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["HSE1", "HSE2", "FCC1", "NAVC1", "R23", "R32"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.5", "FCC1.37", "FCC1.12", "FCC1.13", "NAVC1.5", "NAVC1.6"],
      "nets": ["HSE_IN_FCC", "HSE_OUT_FCC", "HSE_IN_NAVC", "HSE_OUT_NAVC", "Net-(C33-Pad1)", "Net-(C53-Pad1)", "Net-(FCC1-PH0)", "Net-(NAVC1-PH0)", "Net-(NAVC1-PH1)"],
      "observed": "FCC crystal connections go to FCC1 pins 5 and 37 (PE6 and PE7), not its PH0 and PH1 pins. The NAVC crystal nets have no NAVC1 pins on them; NAVC1 PH0 and PH1 instead each connect to a capacitor to ground.",
      "expected": "The 25 MHz crystals should connect to the MCUs' HSE oscillator pins: PH0 and PH1.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_IN_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\")) ... (node (ref \"HSE1\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_OUT_FCC\") (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"37\") (pinfunction \"PE7\")) (node (ref \"R23\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_IN_NAVC\") (node (ref \"C52\") (pin \"1\")) (node (ref \"HSE2\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"Net-(NAVC1-PH0)\") (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PH0\")) (node (ref \"C37\") (pin \"1\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Neither MCU receives its intended external high-speed clock from the fitted crystal. The FCC crystal is routed to unrelated GPIOs, and the NAVC crystal is not connected to the MCU oscillator pins.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are present. The MCUs' main VDD pins are unconnected and the regulated 3.3 V output is isolated from the separate +3V3 net; additionally, FCC UART3 is routed to VCAP pins and both HSE crystal circuits are misconnected."
}

